cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CoTRA in your research, please cite this software using the metadata from this file."
title: "CoTRA: Comprehensive Toolbox for RNA Sequencing Data Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Seemab"
    given-names: "Umair"
    email: "u.seemab@gmail.com"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-21
repository-code: "https://github.com/UmairSeemab/CoTRA"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/UmairSeemab/CoTRA/releases/tag/v1.1.0"
url: "https://github.com/UmairSeemab/CoTRA"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
abstract: >-
  CoTRA is an open-source R/Shiny framework for downstream bulk RNA-seq and
  single-cell RNA-seq analysis. It provides workflows for data import,
  quality control, differential expression, functional enrichment,
  dimensionality reduction, clustering, cell-type annotation, trajectory
  inference, pathway activity analysis, differential abundance,
  cell-cell communication, and report generation. CoTRA supports native
  installation and containerized deployment using Docker to facilitate
  reproducible execution across computing environments.
keywords:
  - "RNA-seq"
  - "single-cell RNA-seq"
  - "bulk RNA-seq"
  - "transcriptomics"
  - "bioinformatics"
  - "R"
  - "Shiny"
  - "Docker"
  - "reproducible research"
  - "containerization"
